WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:04.440
There's no type of fame quite like the one
actors are thrust into after starring in a

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:05.220
Marvel movie.

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:11.600
With international attention can also come
backlash of equal intensity, and sadly, 7-year-old

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:16.070
Avengers: Endgame actress Lexi Rabe is currently
facing the negative effects of being part

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:18.040
of the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:25.700
"What is wrong with you people?"

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:30.480
People have reportedly begun harassing Rabe,
who plays Morgan Stark, the adorable daughter

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:35.160
of Robert Downey Jr.'s Tony Stark and Gwyneth
Paltrow's Pepper Potts in Avengers: Endgame.

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:39.700
Though no specific incidents of stuff have
been explicitly mentioned, it seems that the

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:44.380
harassers became upset over Rabe's behavior
when they saw her in public, finding fault

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:49.399
with her acting, quote, "silly" and evidently
declining to take photos with them.

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:53.860
Rabe and her mother, Jessica, addressed the
unfortunate situation in a video uploaded

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:55.399
to Rabe's Instagram account.

00:00:55.580 --> 00:01:00.480
Jessica Rabe wrote in the caption that, quote,
"yet again Lexi's getting it," and asked

00:01:00.489 --> 00:01:04.570
everyone to please withhold their opinions
about her daughter, so that she can, quote,

00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:05.960
"grow up in the free world."

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:10.980
In the clip, Lexi is seen apologizing for
not being perfect, reminding people that she's

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:12.100
just a young girl:

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:12.840
"Hi.

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:14.020
I'm Lexi Rabe.

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:15.620
And I'm only seven years old.

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:18.280
And I mess up sometimes."

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:20.920
Jessica Rabe elaborated in the caption:

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:24.000
"She's a normal human being and she's a child.

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:28.000
We give her a talking and we give her timeouts
but we don't do that in public.

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:32.340
Sometimes we're rushing from place to place
stressed like everyone else to get to set

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:35.920
on time or work or whatever and we seem a
little grumpy.

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:38.840
I'm sorry if you see us this way but that's
life!

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:42.620
If you ask us for an autograph we [almost
always] say yes.

00:01:42.940 --> 00:01:46.260
If we happen to be having a bad day that might
put us right on the right!

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:47.720
We are not perfect!"

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:53.280
She also noted that, contrary to what some
may believe, Lexi is a well-behaved child,

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:57.859
and if she wasn't, Marvel probably wouldn't
have hired her for Avengers: Endgame.

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:02.620
Rabe's mother then requested that people refrain
from passing judgements or making harsh remarks

00:02:02.630 --> 00:02:07.109
until they have children of their own, and
asked that they realize the Rabe family is,

00:02:07.109 --> 00:02:09.640
quote, "not perfect" and isn't "claiming to
be."

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:13.909
She ended the caption with a heartwarming
reminder that, quote, "My children love me

00:02:13.909 --> 00:02:16.720
and respect me even if they act out sometimes.

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:17.360
Thank you!

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:18.060
Jessica!"

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:23.140
At the end of the video, Lexi, who still had
a smile on her face despite all the backlash,

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:27.189
then tugged on heartstrings when she delivered
the iconic line from Endgame to those who

00:02:27.189 --> 00:02:28.240
have supported her:

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:29.100
"Bye.

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:31.280
love you 3,000."

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:35.920
When it was announced earlier this year
that Orange Is the New Black alum Ruby Rose

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:40.870
had landed the role of Batwoman on the small
screen, disgruntled fans raised their proverbial

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:43.780
pitchforks and claimed that she was the wrong
choice for the part.

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:48.320
The Australian actress deleted her Twitter
account when the negativity became overwhelming.

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:53.299
If cruel criticism can push adult actors to
step away from the limelight, it can only

00:02:53.299 --> 00:02:57.549
be much, much worse for a young girl like
Rabe who has never been exposed to anger and

00:02:57.549 --> 00:02:59.300
animosity like this before.

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:04.150
Thankfully, the Morgan Stark actress seems
to be surrounded by a strong and loving family,

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:07.540
who will keep her spirits high and outside
negativity low.

